config BR2_PACKAGE_QCOM_DSP_FIRMWARE
	bool "qcom-dsp-firmware"
	depends on BR2_aarch64
	help
	  Signed Qualcomm firmware for the Radxa Dragon Q6A, installed
	  under /lib/firmware/qcom at the paths the DTB's `firmware-name`
	  properties (and the drm/msm + venus drivers) point to:

	    remoteproc_cdsp: qcom/qcs6490/radxa/dragon-q6a/cdsp.mbn
	    remoteproc_adsp: qcom/qcs6490/radxa/dragon-q6a/adsp.mbn
	    gpu zap shader:  qcom/qcs6490/a660_zap.mbn
	    gpu sqe/gmu:     qcom/a660_sqe.fw, qcom/a660_gmu.bin
	    venus video:     qcom/vpu-2.0/venus.mbn
	    geni qup:        qcom/qcm6490/qupv3fw.elf

	  Vendored from upstream linux-firmware, where all of these are
	  marked "Licence: Redistributable" (see LICENSE.qcom/NOTICE.qcom).
	  The CDSP image version string MUST match the fastrpc shell from
	  qcom-dsp-shell (CDSP.HT.2.5.c4-00004-KODIAK-1); see
	  blobs/qcom-dsp-firmware/README.md.

	  If the blobs are absent the package installs nothing (the build
	  still succeeds, e.g. for the QEMU smoke test), but the CDSP will
	  NOT come up on real hardware until they are provided.
